---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_31",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 31,
  "text": "<p> [[97.7]] <b>27. HEINRICH OLDENBURG AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[97.8]] London, 10. (20.) August 1670. [26.28.]</b></p>\n<p> [[97.23]] Ampliss^#'o et Consultiss^#'o Viro </p>\n<p> [[97.24]] Dⁿ^#'o Gothofredo Guilielmo Leibnitio J.U.D. etc. Henr. Oldenburg S.P.D. </p>\n<p> [[97.25]] Obtinere a me non potui, Vir Consultiss^#'e, ut Literas tuas 13/23 julii novissimi Moguntia ad\n[[97.26]] me datas silentio praeterirem. Spirant quippe humanitatem non vulgarem; quin et eximiam in\n[[97.27]] provehenda re Philosophica voluntatem testantur. Hujusmodi nova non leviter eos afficiunt\n[[97.28]] juvantque, qui in votis omnino habent, ut omnium gentium viri sagaces et industrii velint studia\n[[98.1]] et exercitia sua ad augendam ornandamque solidam et feracem Philosophiam consociare.\n[[98.2]] Anglia nostra eo inprimis annititur; molitur idem Gallia, et ipsa Italia: nec Germaniam opinamur\n[[98.3]] post principia latere. Tu, Vir Ampliss^#'e, insigniorem pro aetate tua in rebus physicis tum\n[[98.4]] affectum tum progressum significas, eaque de veris Motus Rationibus epistola tua subinnuis,\n[[98.5]] quae Salivam mihi et aliis movent, unicam illam tuam, de qua loqueris, certi motus Universalis\n[[98.6]] in Globo nostro Terr-aqu-aëreo Hypothesin cognoscendi; ex qua scil. omnium, quos in corporibus\n[[98.7]] est deprehendere, motuum ratio, insueta hactenus claritate, reddatur. Virum sane\n[[98.8]] philosophum Te praestabis, si tanti momenti negotium confeceris, remque feceris Societati\n[[98.9]] Regiae gratissimam, si Hypothesis illius summam et rationes exponere non graveris. Idem jam\n[[98.10]] fecit de suis Motus Regulis Hugenius, aliis ipsum in eodem argumento explicando imitantibus;\n[[98.11]] quorum nomina aeque ac meletemata, Cedro digna, nunquam intermorituram in Soc. Regiae\n[[98.12]] Archivis, suum cuique tribuere summopere satagentibus, perennitatem consequuntur: Quod\n[[98.13]] idem tuis eveniet meditationibus et inventis, siquidem in iis edisserendis et communicandis\n[[98.14]] cordatum et facilem Te mihi praebueris. </p>\n<p> [[98.15]] Quam <i>de Arte Combinatoria Dissertationem</i> edidisse Te scribis, ea ad oras nostras necdum\n[[98.16]] pervenit. Eam tanto magis videre opto, quod in ea Te nova non pauca, quaedam etiam\n[[98.17]] profutura observasse sub-indicas. Quae hactenus de Arte illa varii scripserunt, vanam potius\n[[98.18]] loquendi de variis amplitudinem, quam judiciose disserendi et nova solida ac profutura excogitandi\n[[98.19]] rationem docuerunt. </p>\n<p> [[98.20]] Societas nostra in consectandis perpetim Experimentis laborat; unde Sylva suo tempore\n[[98.21]] confertissima succrescet, amplissimam Naturae Historiam complectens, solido et feraci Physices\n[[98.22]] Systemati condendo posteritati forte suffecturam. Quidam ejus Socii de variis varia nuper\n[[98.23]] in lucem emiserunt. Nosti jam, quae Dn. Boylius per aliquot annos feliciter edidit, quorum\n[[98.24]] postrema sunt <i>de Formarum et Qualitatum Origine</i>; de Argumento illo, Num detur <i>absoluta\n[[99.1]] sive perfecta Quies in corporibus</i> etiam solidissimis? <i>De Qualitatibus Systematicis sive Cosmicis:\n[[99.2]] De Suspicionibus Cosmicis: De regionum Sub-terranearum juxta ac Sub-marinarum\n[[99.3]] Temperie, Deque Maris Fundo: quibus accessit Ejusdem Introductio in Historiam de Qualitatibus\n[[99.4]] particularibus</i>. Insuper Dn. Wallisius imprimi nuper curavit duas partes priores <i>Mechanicae,\n[[99.5]] sive Tractatus</i> sui <i>Geometrici de Motu</i>, in quarum prima, de Motu praemittit Generalia,\n[[99.6]] agitque de Gravium descensu, et Motuum Declivitate, speciatim vero de Libra doctrinam tradit:\n[[99.7]] In secunda vero de Centro Gravitatis, ejusque Calculo in figuris quamplurimis Curvi-lineis,\n[[99.8]] atque ex his oriundis Solidis, et Superficiebus curvis. Tertiam et ultimam partem habebimus,\n[[99.9]] quamprimum per Praeli difficultates licebit. Adhaec, D^#'r Barrovius, priori haud impar Author,\n[[99.10]] <i>Lectiones</i> edidit tum <i>Opticas</i> tum <i>Geometricas,</i> a subacti judicii Lectoribus magni aestimatas. </p>\n<p> [[99.11]] In Anatomicis prodiere D^#'r Lowerus <i>de Motu Cordis et Sanguinis</i>; ubi Experimenta istius\n[[99.12]] generis egregia inseruntur: nec non D^#'r^#'i^#'s Thrustoni <i>de Respirationis Usu primario Diatriba</i>. </p>\n<p> [[99.13]] Non ita pridem ad manus meas e Germania pervenerunt chartae quaedam impressae,\n[[99.14]] quarum Titulus; <i>Inventum Novum, Artis et Naturae Connubium, In copulatione Levitatis cum\n[[99.15]] Gravitate, per Artificium Siphonis, Machinae Aquaticae, et Antliae, exhibitum a Georg. Christoph.\n[[99.16]] Wernero, Memmingensi; excusum Augustae A. 1670.</i> Ait Author, Machinam hanc, non\n[[99.17]] modo in minori, sed et majori forma descriptam, in aedibus ipsius, ad quorumvis conditionis\n[[99.18]] hominum servitia prostare. Scire percuperem, num dicta Machina per Germaniam longe lateque\n[[99.19]] innotuerit, et a viris harum rerum callentioribus laudem impetraverit. Multum me Tibi [devinxeris],\n[[99.20]] Vir Spectatiss^#'e, si Memmingae, ubi Inventi Author degit, vel Augustae Vindelicorum,\n[[99.21]] ubi excusus est Libellus, rei et successus veritatem sollicite inquiras, meque de re tota, et de\n[[99.22]] ipsius inprimis artificii ratione perfecte edoceas. </p>\n<p> [[99.23]] Hugenianum Longitudinis, Penduli beneficio, Inventum adhuc in suspenso est. Existimant\n[[99.24]] nonnulli, duo adhuc istius Automati complemento deesse; unum est, quod necdum perpetuo\n[[100.1]] retineatur in situ perpendiculari; alterum, quod multum incommodi ab irregulari motu Aëris\n[[100.2]] ingeratur. Spes tamen est, remedium, defectibus hisce curandis aptum, non adeo esse difficile\n[[100.3]] inventu; quin degit inter nos Vir quidam Mathematicus, qui actu se invenisse remedium illud\n[[100.4]] affirmat, cumque opportunum fuerit, se propalaturum pollicetur. </p>\n<p> [[100.5]] Haec sunt, quae Tuis regerenda hac vice suppetebant. Tu interim, Vir Doctiss^#'e, rem\n[[100.6]] philosophicam ornare et augere perge. Dabam Londini d. 10 Augusti, 1670. </p>\n<p> [[100.7]] P. S. Litteras tuas Dn. Hobbio inscriptas rus, ubi nunc degit, transmisi. Si quid responsi\n[[100.8]] dederit, sine mora ad te curabitur. </p>\n",
  "number": "27.",
  "title": "HEINRICH OLDENBURG AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "London, 10. (20.) August 1670. [26.28.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:27. HEINRICH OLDENBURG AN LEIBNIZ London, 10. (20.) August 1670. [26.28.] Ampliss^#'o et Consultiss^#'o Viro Dⁿ^#'o Gothofredo Guilielmo Leibnitio J.U.D. etc. Henr. Oldenburg S.P.D. Obtinere a me non potui, Vir Consultiss^#'e, ut Literas tuas 13/23 julii novissimi Moguntia ad me datas silentio praet...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>